  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\nThe core idea is to iteratively optimize two complementary strategies for improving the step function representation:\n- Active Optimization: Uses projected gradient descent/Ascent on the correlation vector\n- Strategic Perturbation: Explores non-local features by recursively generating subsequences from the correlation pattern\n\nKey innovations:\n- Dynamically balances local refinement and global exploration\n- Uses adaptive stabilization for gradient learning\n- Maintains feasibility through dual-projection\n- Employs phase-matched oscillation for escaping local optima\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\nRepresentation:\n\ud835\udc9f = {h \u2208 [0,1]\u207f | 1/2 = \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x) dx}\n\nObjective:\nC\u2085 = (2/n) \u00b7 max\u2096 [\u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx]\n\nFormulation cascade:\nPhase I (L1 Relaxation):\nMinimize_\u2225\u03b8\u2225\u2081 \u2265 1/2  max\u2096 |\u27e8\u03c6\u2248h\u27e9\u1d44, \u03c6\u2248h\u27e8_x+k)\u27e9|\nSubject: (Gobuster)\n\nPhase II (Dual Descent):\nMinimize_\u0394 \u2208 \u211d\u207f  max\u2096 (\u27e8h\u1d62 + \u0394 \u00b7 \u0394x, (1-h\u1d62 - \u0394 \u00b7 \u0394x\u207a)\u27e9)\nSubject: 0 \u2264 h\u1d62 + \u0394 \u2264 1, \u2211\u0394 = 0\n\nVictor-Lasker enabled projection for mixed-integer feasibility:\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\nAlgorithm Steps:\ninitialize(h0): Use parent solution (if exists) else initialize randomly\nwhile time budget not exceeded:\n  h <- LocalRefinement(h, phase1=True, sigmas=[0.9,0.01,0.1])\n  h <- LongWavelengthCorrection(h, periods=[50,80,130])\n  h <- ConfidenceEnvelope(h, shrink=\u2207\u209a C\u2085 ||\u2207\u209a defined by Hilbert transform)\n  \u03c6 <- non-negative low-rank factors of spectral decomposition( autocorrelate)\n  h <- MinimumOvershoot(h, candidate)\n\nFeasibility check:\nwhile \u2225h\u2225/n*(2) \u2260 0.5:\n  h <- project_cons_constraint(h)\ndef project_cons_constraint(h):\n  s = np.sum(h)\n  mean_diff = (s - 1) / n\n  h += np.sign(mean_diff) * max(np.clip(|mean_diff|, 0.0)\n  return np.clip(h,0,1)\n\ndef autocorrelate(h):\n  cc = np.correlate(h,1-h,mode=\"full\")\n  return cc*(2/len(h))\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations:\nStart with \u03b8=0.5 in [0,1] for binary candidate (if available)\n\nHyperparameters:\n- Active Learning: Use Hilbert kernel until progress < 0.00001\n- Component Expansion: Add new periodic components (1,2,4) at each significant improvement stage\n- Long-term Correction: Switch to hierarchical search if microstep fails for >3 reps\n- Minimizing Divergence: Use \u03c7\u00b2 criterion for projection\n\n5. Computation budget and robustness:\nBreakdown:\n- Phase I: 30% CPU budget (930 seconds)\n- Phase II: 40% CPU budget (1040 seconds)\n- Perturbation: 20% CPU budget (440 seconds)\n- Safety Check: 10% CPU budget (275 seconds)\n\nFallback procedure:\nOn disagreement between local/gradient and active set predictions:\n  h_fallback = np.random.rand(560)\n  h_fallback = project_cons_constraint(h_fallback)\n\nCancellation handler (inter-process):\n\n6. Validation and return contract:\nBefore finalizing, ensures these properties:\n- 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n- \u222bh dx = 0.5\n- Matches evaluator: max\u2096 [correlation(k)/n] *2 \n\nFinal result format:\n(h, C5, n_points)\nC5 = max(0, (2/n)*np.max(np.correlate(h,1-h,'full')))\n\nJOIN\n//----------------------------------------->",
